{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/artifact.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:06:41.267443Z","id":"c1ce456a956b48529c9e58203775ad77f337fb90ea77e2c51db931f48ba69a50","body":{"detail":"A module-side application from the sidebar island cost about 130 gzip bytes more of the artifact entry's budget and ran later than the head script. The two are kept in step by the unit test 'are laid out by the artifact page's head script before the first paint as applyPrefs lays them out' (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.test.ts), which runs the script against stored values and compares the root's attributes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"d50e7e78b94cf0ae7148f6bf8ed8c9df000af60ce133a0833dfb8f39a6813a32"},"summary":"The drawer's first-paint prefs are applied by an inline head script that mirrors applyPrefs (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.ts), not by the module","tags":["revisit:applyPrefs changes what it sets","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/artifact.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:15:40.529998Z","id":"fe6fe85a13312a1d0fc5967c8e83c13280c0ad650e28f29f49008d65b6a0e104","body":{"detail":"The script's number test `d[k]===+d[k]` is true for Infinity, and JSON.parse(\"1e999\") is Infinity (node: `JSON.parse('{\"w\":1e999}').w===+...` -> true, `+\"px\"` -> \"Infinitypx\"). applyPrefs (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.ts:30) uses Number.isFinite and removes such a value. With `--drawer-w: Infinitypx`, `width: min(var(--drawer-w, 392px), 100% - 320px)` (web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte:61) is invalid at computed-value time, so the docked drawer's width falls back to auto: its content's width, which squeezes the stage. The equivalence test that the alternative c1ce456a relies on (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.test.ts:60) has no overflowing number among its stored values, so the two copies already disagree while the test passes. Failure: localStorage clax.drawer = {\"w\":1e999} (or {\"h\":-1e999} docked at the bottom).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"d50e7e78b94cf0ae7148f6bf8ed8c9df000af60ce133a0833dfb8f39a6813a32"},"suggested_fix":"Test `typeof d[k]==\"number\"&&isFinite(d[k])` in the head script, and add '{\"w\":1e999,\"x\":-1e999}' to the stored values in drawer-model.test.ts:60.","summary":"The clax-drawer head script accepts ±Infinity where applyPrefs drops it, so a stored 1e999 lays the drawer out by an invalid width","tags":["review","review:drawer-layout","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/artifact.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:18:25.686035Z","id":"d1e8514ee109467fdab6878060878fb13abaa23b4860da2976bd975ebc09715d","body":{"detail":"web/shell/artifact.html:7 tests `d[k]===+d[k]`. node: `const d=JSON.parse('{\"w\":1e999,\"h\":-1e999}')` gives w true \"Infinitypx\", h true \"-Infinitypx\". applyPrefs (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.ts:30) uses Number.isFinite and so removes them. The equivalence test's stored values (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.test.ts:59) have no overflowing number. `--drawer-w: Infinitypx` makes `min(var(--drawer-w, 392px), 100% - 320px)` (web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte:61) invalid at computed-value time. Nothing applies the checked prefs on load (see 1895e8b990debb48df4cdd5fcc9b23562717e01391ced86ca6c1d0eac9b5bbf8), so the bad value stays.","kind":"comment","references":"fe6fe85a13312a1d0fc5967c8e83c13280c0ad650e28f29f49008d65b6a0e104","summary":"confirmed: the head script lets an overflowing stored number through, and applyPrefs does not","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/artifact.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:40:58.709695Z","id":"172bfba710b4435b9b162a609727efca01d817ba3f86ef68732d6141311bd405","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8156e76b6","summary":"The clax-drawer head script tests Number.isFinite(d[k]) and applies only the layout and the docked sizes (w, h); applyPrefs lays out the layout as p.layout || \"\" to match. Evidence: the parity test in web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.test.ts now runs the script against {\"w\":1e999,\"x\":-1e999,\"h\":-1e999}, string, boolean, array and object sizes, layout 0, -0, '[]', '\"text\"' and '7', and passes (bazelisk test //web:unit, 1741 passed); //web:bundle_size passes at artifact 64237 of 64243.","supersedes":"fe6fe85a13312a1d0fc5967c8e83c13280c0ad650e28f29f49008d65b6a0e104","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/artifact.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:41:00.788064Z","id":"64d37ea65e78a8afed9ac2eac8e5074ce49daaf485257715e1cca45bcc1109bb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c1ce456a956b48529c9e58203775ad77f337fb90ea77e2c51db931f48ba69a50","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"91d50216db3e69c98b6344989d6b94c33c5c6b762578da4aa8bb1621d7f533d0"},"summary":"The head script now applies the layout and the docked sizes only (w, h), with Number.isFinite; the floating window's sizes come from drawer.svelte.ts, which applies the checked prefs as the controls load. The parity test compares the script with applyPrefs on those fields.","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/artifact.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:10.067730Z","id":"96082b3d7c8e2f8a01b8387673d35b5c669f245c3fb6101cc4b03106ae2edcd4","body":{"detail":"A module-side application from the sidebar island cost about 130 gzip bytes more of the artifact entry's budget and ran later than the head script. The two are kept in step by the unit test 'are laid out by the artifact page's head script before the first paint as applyPrefs lays them out' (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.test.ts), which runs the script against stored values and compares the root's attributes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"91d50216db3e69c98b6344989d6b94c33c5c6b762578da4aa8bb1621d7f533d0"},"summary":"The drawer's first-paint prefs are applied by an inline head script that mirrors applyPrefs (web/shell/src/view/drawer-model.ts), not by the module","supersedes":"c1ce456a956b48529c9e58203775ad77f337fb90ea77e2c51db931f48ba69a50","tags":["revisit:applyPrefs changes what it sets","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
